  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.2.2\"\n  # photo-tagger needs Python >= 3.14, higher than conda-forge's global\n  # python_min, so override it here and reference ${{ python_min }} below.\n  python_min: \"3.14\"\n\npackage:\n  name: photo-tagger\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/photo-tagger/photo_tagger-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: d8f506f3de0cee80f77789436becc4c436bf3ccfcea481cacbe6f892f6dcce1f\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - photo-tagger = photo_tagger.main:app\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - uv-build >=0.11.16,<1.0.0\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - cyclopts >=4.16.1\n    - filelock >=3.29.0\n    - httpx >=0.28.1\n    - loguru >=0.7.3\n    - pillow >=12.2.0\n    - pydantic >=2.13.4\n    - pydantic-ai >=1.104.0\n    - pyexiftool >=0.5.6\n    - rawpy >=0.27.0\n    - rich >=15.0.0\n    # photo-tagger shells out to the `exiftool` binary at runtime to read/write\n    # metadata, so depend on it directly (not just via pyexiftool).\n    - exiftool\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - photo_tagger\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    script:\n      - photo-tagger --help\n\nabout:\n  summary: CLI tool to describe photos and add keywords using AI\n  description: |\n    Photo Tagger is a command-line helper that asks a vision-language model to\n    analyze your photos and writes Lightroom-compatible metadata. By default it\n    keeps your originals untouched by creating XMP sidecar files, but it can\n    embed the updates directly into each photo with --embed-in-photo.\n\n    It requires a running Ollama or LM Studio server that hosts a vision-language\n    model, and the ExifTool binary available on PATH.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  homepage: https://juliobs.com/projects/photo-tagger/\n  repository: https://github.com/jbsilva/photo-tagger\n  documentation: https://github.com/jbsilva/photo-tagger\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jbsilva\n",
